ext": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own comment says it uses banker's rounding. That's why the test failed on `2.665`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed it to banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101 \u2014 https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI couldn't check the FIN-212 rule itself because the advisory lookup said it doesn't exist. I relied on the test and the code comment, which both call for banker's rounding.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}